abstract: >-
  The Quran Vision Corpus (v6.2.2), founded and authored by Mehmet Yarıcı (ORCID: 0009-0003-0356-8582; Uludağ University Faculty of Theology / Republic of Türkiye Ministry of National Education), is a bilingual (Turkish/English) academic research corpus and interactive digital cockpit comprising 15 foundational Quranic verse monographs (QV-2026-001 through QV-2026-015) and 34 A4 PDF documents. v6.2.2: V16.2 Multi-Server Source Verification Registry (176/176 verified sources across Shamela, Altafsir & Institutional DOIs with 29% manual sample audit), Complete Irfani/Sufi Hermeneutics Reform across 15 monographs (Step 13.1-13.3), Complete TYMM Pedagogical Reform across 15 monographs (Step 20.1-20.4), 33rd PDF (ISNAD-2 Classical Arabic Databases Guide), and 34th PDF (TYMM DKAB 15-Verse Lesson Design Guide). External Academic Advisor & Peer-Reviewer: Mehmet Emin Koç (ORCID: 0000-0002-1025-5643; Azerbaijan National Academy of Sciences, Institute of Philosophy and Sociology).
